gest meeting yet to come  tomorrow night with the Chinese  President Xi well that's right and of  course all eyes will be on that meeting  for sure Brett I got to tell you there's  a lot obviously not just at stake but  here's what's going on  president Trump is not at a point now  where he can Bluff I mean in other words  it's time to pony up and what I mean by  that is he can't back away at this point  there's just no way and  so what does that mean well economically  America we know is doing pretty well  that's a good strong hand to go into all  of this with bottom line is if he can  come away with obviously something on  intellectual property theft and also of  all of this force technology transfer in  terms of what the Chinese are doing I  think that's obviously going to be a big  victory for this administration having  said that I think we've got a long road  ahead of us so what I will point one  point out is that over 200 was a 250  billion more in tariffs come January and  that's another issue that John Donald  Trump can raise I plan to ask defense  secretary mattis about a number of  hotspots around the world including  China Morgan here is the president  talking about this meeting yet to come  with President Xi we could make a deal  better be good thing I think they want  to and I think we'd like to and we'll  see but we'll be meeting with President  Xi and for the most part tomorrow I  would say would be a big meeting but in  the meantime people are working our  staff is working and a lot of very  talented people working yeah of laying  the groundwork you know art of the deal  here that's true I don't expect a  full-fledged deal tomorrow I think that  with a problem in the challenge here  which is different for the president  than say what he faced in North Korea is  we really have two competing factions  here clearly the economic and business  interests that side of his  administration would like to get to a  deal sooner rather than later because  they'r